@@ -2,6 +2,26 @@
 
 This package enables ESC testing with a turtlebot with a rotating sensor frame. This package includes several ROS2 nodes built specifically to work with the sensors and servo motors used in the vehicle construction. Please use the turtlebot launch file to configure and start and experiment. This package is intended to be used with ros_esc, ros_esc_interfaces, and extremum-seeking packages from the DSIM Lab Gitlab.
 
+## Phase 09 selected GESC plus Gaussian profile
+
+The selected physical workflow uses the existing launch and node owners with
+the cumulative Phase 08 runtime through v8.12. The new
+`gesc_gaussian_counted_two_source_voltage.bash` wrapper selects either the
+primary or secondary evaluation metadata, requires a stable serial
+device-by-id and reviewed calibration, and runs the launch inside the sole
+`ros_esc record_run` readiness/recording owner.
+
+The checked-in Phase 09 calibration is intentionally uncalibrated and blocks
+the wrapper. Do not mark it motion-ready from simulator values. Live Pi
+transfer, stationary calibration, rotating-frame checks, emergency-stop
+rehearsal, and motion all require later explicit authorization.
+
+The selected robust graph uses wheel/IMU-backed `/odom`, monitors `/imu`, and
+keeps exactly one `/cmd_vel` publisher. Vicon and the legacy CSV collector are
+legacy-only; evaluator coordinates and lamp roles never enter control. The
+operator ends a managed run with `Ctrl+C`, which lets readiness fall false,
+records final zero commands, finalizes the bag, and performs scoped cleanup.
+
 ![Visualization of the turtlebot vehicle with a rotating sensor frame.](/turtlebot3_rotating_sensor_model.jpg)
 
 ## Author Information
