-
-To view active ros processes use the following command
-```
-user@machine:~$  ps aux | grep ros
-```
-The process ID is the second entry in the line for each process
-
-To view the process command name, make use of the process id {PID} and the following command
-```
-ps -p {PID} -o comm=
-```
+## To stop a managed experiment
 
-To kill that process with that command name {CMD_NAME} use the following command
-```
-pkill -9 {CMD_NAME}
-```
\ No newline at end of file
+Use `Ctrl+C` in the terminal that owns `record_run`. Allow its bounded
+readiness-false, stop, final-zero, bag-finalization, and descendant-cleanup
+sequence to finish. Do not use broad process-name `pkill -9` commands; they
+can bypass final-zero evidence and affect unrelated ROS processes.
