+# Photoresistor node
+
+This existing physical owner reads the Arduino protocol
+`v: <float>, r: <float>` over a bounded serial connection. It preserves the
+legacy `StampedFloat64MultiArray` output and its minimization convention:
+measured voltage is positive, while the legacy raw cost is `-V`.
+
+For the Phase 09 robust profile it can also publish
+`ros_esc_interfaces/msg/CostBreakdown` on
+`/gesc_gaussian/source_cost`. The typed message is single-channel physical
+data with `raw_sensor_value=[V]` and `raw_cost=[-V]`. It is not published until
+the supplied calibration is both `calibrated` and `motion_ready`.
+
+```bash
+ros2 run turtlebot3_vehicle_nodes photoresistor_node \
+  INPUT_TIMEKEEPER_TOPIC OUTPUT_TOPIC Voltage \
+  --serial-port /dev/serial/by-id/REVIEWED_DEVICE \
+  --baud-rate 9600 \
+  --serial-timeout-sec 0.50 \
+  --publish-source-cost True \
+  --source-cost-topic /gesc_gaussian/source_cost \
+  --calibration-file /path/to/reviewed_calibration.yaml
 ```
